                    response: We train a binary classifier                      
                    by fine-tuning only the final layer of                      
                    a pretrained ResNet-18 to distinguish                       
                    malignant lesions from benign and                           
                    non-neoplastic cases. Images are                            
                    resized to 224×224 and augmented with                       
                    horizontal flips, and we use standard                       
                    ImageNet normalization. We perform                          
                    5-fold stratified cross-validation on                       
                    the malignant vs. non-malignant labels                      
                    and report the AUC-ROC for each fold                        
                    and their mean. A reusable predict()                        
                    function is provided to compute                             
                    malignancy probabilities on new                             
